    "configuration": {
      "type": "object",
      "title": "SFTP",
      "properties": {
        "sftp.defaultProtocol": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "sftp",
            "ftp"
          ],
          "default": "sftp",
          "order": 1,
          "markdownDescription": "Transfer protocol assumed when a server config (`.vscode/sftp.json` or an in-path `.sftp.json`) does not set `protocol`.\n\n- `sftp` — file transfer tunnelled over SSH (default port `22`). Encrypted, key/agent auth, the usual choice.\n- `ftp` — plain FTP (default port `21`). Use `secure` in the config for FTPS.\n\nAny server config can override this with its own `\"protocol\"`."
        },
        "sftp.defaultAuthMethod": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "agent",
            "key",
            "password",
            "interactive"
          ],
          "enumDescriptions": [
            "Use a running SSH agent (recommended). Socket from sftp.defaultAgentSocket; falls back to a password prompt if no agent is reachable.",
            "Use the private key file at sftp.defaultPrivateKeyPath.",
            "Prompt for a password on every new connection.",
            "Keyboard-interactive auth (one-time codes / 2FA)."
          ],
          "default": "agent",
          "order": 2,
          "markdownDescription": "How SFTP authenticates a server whose config declares **no** authentication of its own — no `agent`, `privateKeyPath`, `password` or `interactiveAuth`. A config that sets any of those is used as-is and ignores this setting.\n\n- **`agent`** *(default)* — authenticate through the SSH agent named by `#sftp.defaultAgentSocket#` (default `$SSH_AUTH_SOCK`). Nothing secret goes in your config files, `ssh-add`-ed keys and agents forwarded over SSH both work. If the agent is not reachable, SFTP logs a warning and falls back to a password prompt.\n- **`key`** — use the private key at `#sftp.defaultPrivateKeyPath#`. Falls back to a password prompt if that setting is empty.\n- **`password`** — prompt for a password each time a connection is opened.\n- **`interactive`** — keyboard-interactive authentication, for servers that ask for a one-time code / 2FA challenge.\n\nApplied per server on every connection, so changing it takes effect without reloading."
        },
        "sftp.defaultAgentSocket": {
          "type": "string",
          "default": "$SSH_AUTH_SOCK",
          "order": 3,
          "markdownDescription": "Where to find the SSH agent when `#sftp.defaultAuthMethod#` is `agent` (also used whenever a config sets `\"agent\"` to a `$NAME` value).\n\n- **`$SSH_AUTH_SOCK`** *(default)* — read the environment variable of that name. This is the standard agent socket exported by `ssh-agent`, GNOME Keyring, `gpg-agent`, the 1Password / Bitwarden SSH agents, a WSL agent, or an agent **forwarded over SSH** (`ssh -A`).\n- **`$OTHER_VARIABLE`** — read a different environment variable.\n- **`pageant`** — on Windows, use PuTTY's Pageant.\n- **an absolute path** — a specific agent socket (e.g. `/run/user/1000/keyring/ssh`).\n\nIf the named environment variable is empty, SFTP logs a warning and prompts for a password instead of failing."
        },
        "sftp.defaultPrivateKeyPath": {
          "type": "string",
          "default": "",
          "order": 4,
          "markdownDescription": "Absolute path to a private key file, used when `#sftp.defaultAuthMethod#` is `key` and a server config does not set its own `privateKeyPath`.\n\n`~/` is expanded to your home directory, e.g. `~/.ssh/id_ed25519`. Leave empty to fall back to a password prompt when no key is configured. For an encrypted key, set `passphrase` in the individual config (or `\"passphrase\": true` to be prompted)."
        },
        "sftp.defaultIgnore": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "default": [
            ".git",
            ".svn",
            ".hg",
            ".DS_Store",
            "Thumbs.db",
            ".vscode",
            ".sftp.json",
            ".sftpignore"
          ],
          "order": 5,
          "markdownDescription": "Central ignore list — gitignore-style patterns that are never uploaded or downloaded — applied to any server that does not define ignores of its own.\n\nFor a given server the ignore list comes from the **first** of these that exists (they are **not** merged):\n\n1. `\"ignoreFile\"` in the config → that file (a relative path is resolved from the workspace root)\n2. `\"ignore\": [ … ]` in the config → that list\n3. a **`.sftpignore`** file in the same folder as the `.sftp.json` (or next to `.vscode/sftp.json`) → that file\n4. **this setting**\n\nSo: put shared rules here, drop a `.sftpignore` next to a specific `.sftp.json` to override them for that subtree, or keep an inline `\"ignore\"` in a config for a one-off."
        },
        "sftp.defaultUploadOnSave": {
          "type": "boolean",
          "default": false,
          "order": 6,
          "markdownDescription": "Default for `uploadOnSave`. When `true`, saving a file anywhere inside a synced folder immediately uploads it. Override per server with `\"uploadOnSave\"` in the config."
        },
        "sftp.defaultUseTempFile": {
          "type": "boolean",
          "default": false,
          "order": 7,
          "markdownDescription": "Default for `useTempFile`. When `true`, an upload is written to a temporary file on the server and then renamed into place, so a half-written file is never served (useful for live web roots). Override per server with `\"useTempFile\"`."
        },
        "sftp.defaultDownloadOnOpen": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "never",
            "confirm",
            "always"
          ],
          "enumDescriptions": [
            "Never fetch the server copy when a file is opened.",
            "Ask each time a file is opened whether to fetch the server copy.",
            "Always fetch the server copy when a file is opened (can overwrite local edits)."
          ],
          "default": "never",
          "order": 8,
          "markdownDescription": "Default for `downloadOnOpen` — whether opening a file first pulls the server's version. `confirm` asks; `always` overwrites the local file silently. Override per server with `\"downloadOnOpen\": true | false | \"confirm\"`."
        },
        "sftp.defaultConnectTimeout": {
          "type": "number",
          "default": 10000,
          "order": 9,
          "markdownDescription": "Default for `connectTimeout`, in **milliseconds** — how long to wait for a connection to be established before giving up. Raise it for slow or distant servers. Override per server with `\"connectTimeout\"`."
        },
        "sftp.defaultInteractiveAuth": {
          "type": "boolean",
          "default": false,
          "order": 10,
          "markdownDescription": "Default for `interactiveAuth`. When `true`, keyboard-interactive authentication is always offered — for servers that prompt for a one-time code / 2FA challenge **in addition to** a key or agent.\n\nThis is distinct from `#sftp.defaultAuthMethod#` `interactive`, which only applies when a config has no authentication at all. Override per server with `\"interactiveAuth\"` (a boolean, or an array of answers to send automatically)."
        },
        "sftp.defaultConcurrency": {
          "type": "number",
          "default": 4,
          "order": 11,
          "markdownDescription": "Default for `concurrency` — how many files are transferred in parallel during a folder / project upload or download. Lower it (e.g. `1`) for servers that rate-limit or drop parallel SFTP channels; raise it for fast links. FTP always uses `1`. Override per server with `\"concurrency\"`."
        },
        "sftp.defaultPlaceholderFileSize": {
          "type": "string",
          "default": "1GB",
          "pattern": "^\\s*(\\d+(\\.\\d+)?\\s*([bB]|[kKmMgGtT][bB])?)?\\s*$",
          "order": 12,
          "markdownDescription": "Default for `placeholder.fileSize`. A remote file larger than this is **not downloaded**; an empty `<name>.placeholder` marker is created locally instead, and while it exists (and the real file does not) that name is skipped in both directions. Accepts bytes or a unit, e.g. `500MB`, `1.5GB`. Default `1GB`; empty = off. Delete the marker and **Download** the file (or just copy the real file in) to get it; a 0-byte marker next to a real file is deleted on the next sync."
        },
        "sftp.defaultPlaceholderDirectorySize": {
          "type": "string",
          "default": "10GB",
          "pattern": "^\\s*(\\d+(\\.\\d+)?\\s*([bB]|[kKmMgGtT][bB])?)?\\s*$",
          "order": 13,
          "markdownDescription": "Default for `placeholder.directorySize`. A remote folder whose total size (recursive, ignored files excluded) is larger than this is not downloaded; a `<name>.placeholder` marker is created instead. Measuring lists the folder over the connection, stopping as soon as the limit is passed. Accepts bytes or a unit, e.g. `2GB`. Default `10GB`; empty = off."
        },
        "sftp.defaultPlaceholderSuffix": {
          "type": "string",
          "default": ".placeholder",
          "pattern": "^[^\\\\/]+$",
          "order": 14,
          "markdownDescription": "Default for `placeholder.suffix` — appended to the original file/folder name to form the marker. Files with this suffix are never transferred while placeholders are enabled."
        },
        "sftp.printDebugLog": {
          "type": "boolean",
          "default": false,
          "description": "print debug log on sftp output channel.(reload vscode when change this)"
        },
        "sftp.debug": {
          "type": "boolean",
          "default": false,
          "description": "print debug log on sftp output channel.(reload vscode when change this)"
        },
        "sftp.downloadWhenOpenInRemoteExplorer": {
          "type": "boolean",
          "default": false,
          "description": "\"Download\" instead of \"View Content\" when open file in Remote Explorer"
        },
        "sftp.autoUpdate": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "auto",
            "prompt",
            "off"
          ],
          "default": "auto",
          "order": 30,
          "markdownDescription": "How to handle a newer build found on an `#sftp.updateFeeds#`. `auto`: download, install and offer a reload. `prompt`: ask first. `off`: only the **SFTP: Check for Updates** command checks."
        },
        "sftp.updateFeeds": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "default": [
            "https://github.com/will-lottkowitz-prism/sftp-custom/releases/latest/download/latest.json"
          ],
          "order": 31,
          "markdownDescription": "Locations of a `latest.json` release manifest, tried in order (first hit wins). Each entry is an `http(s)` URL or a local/synced folder path."
        },
        "sftp.updateCheckIntervalHours": {
          "type": "number",
          "default": 6,
          "order": 32,
          "markdownDescription": "Minimum hours between automatic update checks. `0` checks on every activation. The **Check for Updates** command ignores this."
        }
      }
    },
